 humans refugees trying to escape the  silent war but that's been done so how  do they do something bit different with  that but it makes sense that would be  one of the perspectives  one perspective is obviously going to be  a cylon perspective the attackers well  to consider what the third aspect could  be we have to consider the cylinders on  what we know  right so the cylons were constructed by  man  there was a war they left the cylons  believe in one god they're monotheistic  the humans believe in multiple gods an  interesting twist that ronald d moore  found quite funny when he did the  original series because normally in  these types of things  the  people that believe in multiple gods are  the bad guys and the good guys are the  ones that believe in one god  so and it's a little twister but the  silence believe that they need to  eradicate humanity before they can  really become in touch with their god  because they believe  that god made humanity and made them  imperfect but then  through humanity built the cylons to be  closer to that perfection now the cylons  have at times tried to create hybrids  that are part human part cylon  there was a whole breeding program by  one of the seven  and even as far back as the first cylon  war the silence were trying to do this  the cylon hybrids that control and are  the heart of all base stars originally  were humans taken kidnapped during the  original asylum war and basically  experimented upon  the cylons though had gone on to  continue that experimentation through  sexual hybridization actually breeding  hybrids with humans  so could it be that the third  perspective is one of these hybrids  perhaps a hybrid on a base star reaches  a different kind of consciousness  because we also know that within the  cylon hierarchy they didn't always agree  for example number two or leo von conoy  said that the hybrids could hear god  that they were closer to god somehow  now if they believe that as part of  their religion  